320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (This Primer is designed to support Malaysian boards, directors and senior management in exercising informed oversight of AI adoption and governance. It is not intended to turn board members into technical specialists. Rather, it provides a practical reference to help boards understand AI-related opportunities and risks, ask the right strategic questions and consider whether AI use cases are aligned with organisational purpose, risk appetite, ethical considerations and applicable legal and governance obligations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (The Primer may also be useful for organisations at different stages of AI maturity, from those beginning to explore AI use cases to those deploying AI systems across business functions. In applying this Primer, boards should consider whether AI initiatives create measurable value, whether associated risks are proportionately managed, and whether appropriate governance, validation, monitoring and accountability arrangements are in place before material deployment or scaling.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
