/P 204 0 R
/E (Deployment is not the end of the AI lifecycle but the beginning of continuous oversight. AI systems should be monitored for performance drift, bias emergence, and unintended consequences. Organisations should prepare for lifecycle closure \(i.e., decommissioning or retiring a system\) as much as for deployment. This should include proportionate safeguards for the secure handling, retention or disposal of related data, model assets and system records. This requires logging mechanisms, escalation pathways for incidents, and procedures for updating or sunsetting AI systems responsibly.)
/Pg 29 0 R
/K [1]
>>
