/P 207 0 R
/E (If AI touches personal data at any stage \(inputs, training, outputs\), PDPA obligations apply: boards should expect governance around notice and consent, vendor disclosures, and robust security and retention safeguards. Under the Personal Data Protection \(Amendment\) Act 2024 [Act A1727], biometric data is expressly treated as sensitive personal data. Boards should also anticipate increasing regulatory focus on automated decision-making and profiling through guidance and related instruments.)
/Pg 32 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
