/P 209 0 R
/E (A project risk alone could indicate a flawed model, unsafe system behaviour, or poor data quality. However, when similar gaps appear consistently across projects or functions, they may indicate programme-level weaknesses in governance, oversight and risk management. )
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
550 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 209 0 R
/E (Boards should therefore assess not only how individual projects are managed, but whether the organisation has the capacity, culture and accountability measures to prevent such risks from scaling across the enterprise. Boards should also consider whether particular sectors, products or use cases carry additional legal, ethical or domain-specific requirements.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
