/E (Hence, AI applications should be assessed against this risk appetite. Those that align with organisational values and tolerances may be adopted with proportionate controls, while higher risk or unfamiliar applications may require enhanced oversight, more rigorous testing, or, where appropriate, retrenchment. The following sets out a selective and non-exhaustive list of AI risks adapted from the MIT AI Risk Repository. Not all risks will apply equally across sectors or use cases, and their relevance should be assessed in context, including the likelihood and severity of potential harm and the effectiveness of existing controls.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [7]
>>
